       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **Requested:** ibuprofen 1600 mg PO four times daily, which is 6,400 mg/day.\n- **Limits:** The usual maximum for adults is 3,200 mg/day under supervision, with single doses of 800 mg or less. This order is twice the daily maximum, and each dose is twice the usual single-dose limit. That raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum for inflammatory conditions)\n- **400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours** (typical for pain or fever)\n- **1600 mg total per day**, divided into smaller doses\n\nIf you want the order exactly as written, tell me the clinical reason and I'll enter it with a note. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
